Subject: dcomp: forward messages of an orphaned target subclass to the real wndproc

When the last composition target for an HWND is released while dxgi is still
subclassed on top of us, our unhook is skipped and the __wine_dcomp_target
property is removed, but dxgi keeps calling this procedure as its saved
original. The subclass then has no target and sent everything - including all
mouse input - to DefWindowProc. The window kept painting, because the dcomp
side blits independently of the WndProc, so the symptom is an editor that
renders perfectly and is completely input-dead. Hit with JUCE 8 / SWAM editors,
which recreate device and target over a window's lifetime.

Forward to __wine_dcomp_real_wndproc instead. That property is already
maintained by CreateTargetForHwnd on this base, is set once per window and
never removed, so it still holds the application's own procedure at the point
the subclass is orphaned.

This replaces the five-hunk version this patch carried against the 11.13 base,
which maintained a parallel __wine_dcomp_origproc property. That scheme is
redundant here: on this base a second CreateTargetForHwnd never re-subclasses,
the new target inherits orig_wndproc from its predecessor, and
__wine_dcomp_real_wndproc already provides the window-lifetime fallback.

Reported upstream and adopted by giang17 as ba291fb4f20 on d2d1-dcomp-11.0,
which is not in the d2d1-dcomp-11.14 snapshot this base is taken from - the
orphan branch there still returns DefWindowProcW. Drop this patch once a
snapshot carrying that commit is picked up.

diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/device.c b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
index 627d281..f8a79cb 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -3226,7 +3226,21 @@ static LRESULT CALLBACK dcomp_target_wndproc(HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam,
     WNDPROC orig_wndproc;
 
     if (!target)
+    {
+        /* The subclass outlived its target: the last target was released while
+         * dxgi sat subclassed on top, so our unhook was skipped, the target
+         * property is gone, and dxgi still calls this procedure as its saved
+         * original.  Swallowing here sends every message - including all mouse
+         * input - to DefWindowProc, while the window keeps painting because the
+         * dcomp side blits independently of the WndProc.  The result is an
+         * editor that renders perfectly and is completely input-dead.  Forward
+         * to the window-lifetime original instead. */
+        WNDPROC real_wndproc = (WNDPROC)GetPropW(hwnd, dcomp_real_wndproc_prop);
+
+        if (real_wndproc)
+            return CallWindowProcW(real_wndproc, hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam);
         return DefWindowProcW(hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam);
+    }
 
     orig_wndproc = target->orig_wndproc;
 
